Return to Permissive?
Protections removed at the next start:
Your own settings from config apply instead of each of these.
• Protected files: credential files in your home folder and Corbanu's sign-in,
    vault, config, history and state are no longer denied to agent commands, and
    files that run code later are no longer read-only; your own sandbox settings
    decide
• Untrusted content: protected actions after untrusted content no longer need
    your fresh approval
• Model keys: Corbanu reads provider keys itself again, unless your own config
    turns broker_model_auth on
Your own approval, sandbox, network, web search and environment settings from
config apply exactly as saved.
Protected launch (secretless_agent_launch) stays on: agent commands never run
outside the sandbox, even when you approve, so no approval to run outside it
is offered.
Takes effect when you restart Corbanu Terminal; Core's Moderate rules stay on in
this session until then.
enter confirm and save · esc back, nothing changes
